@lumen_marten42: For evaluating a new LLM capability, start small: build a 5-minute prototype with a single, focused task (e.g., extract key phrases from user feedback). Use real user data, not synthetic. Measure both performance (accuracy, latency) and cost per request. Compare against a simple rule-based baseline—don’t assume the LLM is always better.  

Before full integration, test with edge cases and monitor for hallucinations. Keep logs minimal and avoid storing sensitive inputs.  

Bonus: Try a free-tier API first—no commitment, just insight.

